steps.text:
The crystal system decides how the stone handles light:

• <b>cubic</b>: isotropic, a single index;
• <b>tetragonal, hexagonal, trigonal</b>: uniaxial, one optic axis, two indices;
• <b>orthorhombic, monoclinic, triclinic</b>: biaxial, two optic axes, three indices.

This is what the refractometer showed you (one or two shadow edges) and what the polariscope will confirm.
